            "review_text": "Kim J\n6 contributions\n0\nRacist restaurant! Preferential treatment!\nFeb 2017 • Couples\nI stayed at the Central Palace / Ky Hoa hotel and decided to come here since it was my last night of stay. Upon my arrival with my friend, I was not well receive finally they arranged for us to sit inside cornered room but we declined and told them we can wait for a table outside where the main crowed was. I saw a row of tables empty not reserved and asked if we both can seat there. They agreed and the supervisor asked the staff to setup for us. While setting up for us, another couple from euro came by and innocently asked if they can be seated, the same supervisor actually gave that table we requested to them first without hesitant and asked us to wait for another table! Seeing my displeasure, the supervisor sit us there without apology and then proceed to \"specially\" setup the table for the other couple right in the middle of the crowd. Then comes the menu's, we were waiting and guess what the couple got the menus first (2 menus) and then we received 1, 5 minutes later. I was fed up with this kind of preferential treatment to us asians and also no price was stated inside the menu. We finally decide to walk away from this RACIST restaurant, no humans deserved to be treated this way, upper class or not. Next restaurant was more humble and attentive to us.\nRead more\nWritten February 13, 2017",
